{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece","id":1291808,"title":"Third Edition Raksi: Less Monstrous But Far More Villainous: An Opinion Piece","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-25T06:32:56-08:00","id":1291808,"title":"Third Edition Raksi: Less Monstrous But Far More Villainous: An Opinion Piece","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Part 1: How it started.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In a time that was long before the First Age, in the First Edition, Raksi was described as living as a blood-goddess. We are told that her apemen and &quot;Wyld vassals&quot; roam the area looking for tribute. The locals attempt suicide rather than face the horrors of Mahalanka, because Raksi has an insatiable thirst for the heart's blood of youths. She also views the people of the Ten Tribes who are descendants of Sperimin as her property. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This was a time when Lunars were closer to their cousins in the Old World of Darkness. They could be any sort of animal, sure, but territory was of unparalleled importance. Therefore you never encroached on Mahalanka, &quot;the City of a Thousand Golden Delights&quot; as it's translated, without permission. We do see that she is willing to mentor other Lunars, through the example of Dark Eyes, but her monstrous behavior is mostly just tolerated because she is shahan-ya.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shahan-ya meant something different back then, however. In Third Edition, the Shahan-ya are the faction leaders and policy setters for the Silver Pact. In First Edition, being shahan-ya is being the most respected, but that's it. This is evident in Ma-Ha-Suchi merely being murr-ya, still revered but a step down. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And that's all we really know about First Editition Raksi. She probably was a sorcerer given she was an elder No-Moon. She probably had a hand in the creation of the Lunar Tattoos, but she wasn't yet the architect behind them. All we are told is a vague, the No Moons did it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Part 2: Dawn of the Second Ed</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As one edition changed to another so did Raksi's role within the story. She became more important to the Silver Pact even as her interest in it waned. She was one of the greatest sorcerers in the fallen age, if not the greatest. She invented the caste-fixing tattoos, but she also became more explicitly monstrous. The Chimera, a mere concept in the previous edition, was for better or worse added to an refined. Raksi was not a Chimera, but she hovered at the edge. The Wyld had twisted her. Her human true form was locked into a body forever 16 years old, and her fingers bent backwards. Her most troubling mutations were mental, however. Her favorite food became human flesh and hated beautiful things, and her enjoyment of torturing became well known. There is also the first mention of one of the things Raksi has become infamous for, eating babies.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Part 3: Now and the Future</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The manuscript previews tell us, for now at least, that &quot;her depraved self-indulgence and unflinching cruelty&quot; are an act. Sure she still eats children, commits torture, and many other atrocities, but she does so because &quot;she believes that soft-hearted or idealistic Lunars must be made ready to confront the atrocities committed in the course of the Pact\u2019s vendetta against the Realm.&quot; We are given some conflicting information, however. She didn't teach the soft-hearted Weyna Who-Sees-Much anything of the sort when Weyna objects to eating a child. Raksi gives her respect and the child for this instead, and she now considers the baby her grandchild. I can only guess that Raksi's monstrosity being an act steams from the writers wanting her to be available as a mentor. This show in the change from a scant reference of Dark Eyes to lording her magical acumen over prospective students to &quot;[drawing] many students. At any given time, she\u2019s likely to have a small coterie of adherents studying under her.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Part 4: Bringing it Together</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I argue that the effort to make Raksi less of an unapproachable monster, which was done successfully, has made her the most morally reprehensible and Villainous she has ever been. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First, it's worth noting that Lunar Chimeras aren't a thing in Third Edition because the Lunars losing their old castes isn't a Wyld affliction like it had been for the previous two editions. Now it was an act of self-determination, a prominent theme in the new Lunars book. So we can assume that she acts for no other reason than her will. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Raksi's monstrosity is an act to teach other Lunars, sure, but she still commits these acts. Her story isn't one of decreeing the baby will be cut in half to find its true mother. Her story is one of cutting the baby apart and determining who gets to eat which portion. &quot; Raksi revels in being Raksi.&quot; That means that &quot;she enjoys living up to the rumors new adherents have heard of her, &quot;sure but doesn't that also mean she enjoys engaging in the activities that spark those rumors? She may serve babies on a platter to guests to shock them and not because they are her favorite food, but she still revels in it, no matter how exaggerated her &quot;facade of monstrosity&quot; supposedly is. No matter how much it's an &quot;act&quot; she still does these things for real, really vivisecting prisoners of war, really forcing her champions to engage in blood sport, and all the while &quot; Raksi revels in being Raksi.&quot; The stated reason for her &quot;act&quot; is to teach, but as I had mentioned above she is willing to ignore that reason on a whim. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We didn't really know enough about Raksi in First Ed. to call her much of a monster. Sure, she had a heart's blood addiction and was a bit of a tyrant, but she wasn't mentioned more than a few brief sections. In Second Ed. she was broken, and being broken turned her into a monster. In Third Ed. she is set to be choosing the path of a monster and therefore is a villain. Can you honestly tell that she is any better than The Mask of Winters or any other villain?<br /> <br /> Edit: I stand corrected. There is one mention of baby eating in the First Edition book.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24938,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24938-mmooney","user":"Mmooney","date":". 02-25-2019, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24938-mmooney","name":"Mmooney","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T06:48:21-08:00","id":1291809,"title":"","content":"They're gonna need the Mask of Winters to be a viable mentor for abyssals. So no, they're probably about the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:11:48-08:00","id":1291813,"title":"","content":"The baby-eating thing is at least as old as the First Edition Lunar's book, where it factors into a pre-chapter fiction and artwork depicting the &quot;feast&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:44:23-08:00","id":1291830,"title":"","content":"Reminds me a lot of Mottom from Kill Six Billion Demons in that she tells herself that her monstrous acts are necessary but she primarily does them but because she's too self-obsessed, too lazy to change, and too afraid of what will happen if she stops. Still a terrible character flaw, but less &quot;For the Evulz&quot; and more dysfunctional failed hero. She's a teacher alright, but she's also a cautionary tale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:53:26-08:00","id":1291833,"title":"","content":"To be frank, I agree with this, except for one thing: that this is a bad thing. Raksi is very much the evil part of the Silver Pact, the rakhasha queen. Mighty, intelligent, and completely unapologetic. She knows she's the bad guy, and loves it.<br /> <br /> Quite simply, Raksi-the-Monster was wasted potential, a video game boss riven by dementia and little more than a fight waiting in the wings. Raksi-the-Villain is raw, primal power attached to a nuclear dynamo of a mind and a living nightmare that nonetheless offers benefits for working with her.<br /> <br /> I hate the monster. I love to hate the villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:55:42-08:00","id":1291834,"title":"","content":"A villain doesn't need to be doing it &quot;For the Evulz&quot; to still be a villain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24938-mmooney","name":"Mmooney","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:58:25-08:00","id":1291835,"title":"","content":"Leliel I don't recall saying that it's a bad thing, merely that it is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24938-mmooney","name":"Mmooney","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T08:03:18-08:00","id":1291836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mmooney</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291835#post1291835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leliel I don't recall saying that it's a bad thing, merely that it is</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry. I misread.<br /> <br /> And I agree. Thankfully, I don't think Raksi does; she put on the mask of being a monster and found she liked it. She always has an agenda, but revels in the means she takes to get there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T08:06:14-08:00","id":1291837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mmooney</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291834#post1291834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A villain doesn't need to be doing it &quot;For the Evulz&quot; to still be a villain</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I never implied so, but powerful &quot;for the Evulz&quot; villains tend to be really boring or frustrating to deal with because their power far outstrips the level of dramatic narrative you can wring from them, particularly when their M.O. is to sit around being passively awful without any greater agenda (this isn't always the case, but they need to be custom made to fit the narrative). More complex, humanly flawed villains, even if they're not directly sympathetic, are more interesting. Narrative-wise there's not much you can do with a sociopath, because they're a sociopath, they can't change and never had the potential be anything else other than a pathological glitch in the human condition(again, they can be done well, but it needs to be specific to the story's themes, which, in a roleplaying game, is a bit difficult because players inject their own themes). They'd be an obstacle to overcome, but not a full on person.<br /> <br /> Humanized villains offer more avenues for the plot to progress along and more satisfying conclusions than &quot;this person is an inherently horrible shit, lets kill them and get back to more important things.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 02-25-2019, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T08:23:07-08:00","id":1291843,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but the idea of the writers thinking the majority of players would consider Raksi as a mentor only has me pondering whether they'd give <i>Lilith</i> the same treatment. Yikes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T08:24:49-08:00","id":1291844,"title":"","content":"What's wrong with Lilith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T08:35:12-08:00","id":1291846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291844#post1291844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's wrong with Lilith?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they can retool her like they did Raksi? Not much. I had about an hour-long conversation with a friend Saturday about how badly Dreams wrecked her, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T09:26:38-08:00","id":1291858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291843#post1291843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but the idea of the writers thinking the majority of players would consider Raksi as a mentor only has me pondering whether they'd give <i>Lilith</i> the same treatment. Yikes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Restoring Lilith to her First Edition coolness was an important personal goal. You'll see her in Chapter Nine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T09:50:10-08:00","id":1291865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291837#post1291837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And I never implied so, but powerful &quot;for the Evulz&quot; villains tend to be really boring or frustrating to deal with because their power far outstrips the level of dramatic narrative you can wring from them, particularly when their M.O. is to sit around being passively awful without any greater agenda (this isn't always the case, but they need to be custom made to fit the narrative). More complex, humanly flawed villains, even if they're not directly sympathetic, are more interesting. Narrative-wise there's not much you can do with a sociopath, because they're a sociopath, they can't change and never had the potential be anything else other than a pathological glitch in the human condition(again, they can be done well, but it needs to be specific to the story's themes, which, in a roleplaying game, is a bit difficult because players inject their own themes). They'd be an obstacle to overcome, but not a full on person.<br /> <br /> Humanized villains offer more avenues for the plot to progress along and more satisfying conclusions than &quot;this person is an inherently horrible shit, lets kill them and get back to more important things.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, given the times we live in, my taste for and capacity to believe in the villain with some deep, compelling ideological motivation or formative tragic backstory has waned significantly. <br /> <br /> As for Raksi, I think one thing that's useful about how she's written up is that the conditions in which the worst things that she does happen can have their frequency adjusted to taste. Either in terms of &quot;there's no much call to do them because she's effectively gotten the message across that her opponents she keep out of the TCZ&quot; or &quot;serving up a baby is something she did, like, twice, amongst all the other crap she could pull, but it's a reputation that sticks&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T10:15:07-08:00","id":1291870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291865#post1291865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, given the times we live in, my taste for and capacity to believe in the villain with some deep, compelling ideological motivation or formative tragic backstory has waned significantly.<br /> <br /> As for Raksi, I think one thing that's useful about how she's written up is that the conditions in which the worst things that she does happen can have their frequency adjusted to taste. Either in terms of &quot;there's no much call to do them because she's effectively gotten the message across that her opponents she keep out of the TCZ&quot; or &quot;serving up a baby is something she did, like, twice, amongst all the other crap she could pull, but it's a reputation that sticks&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not saying that villains should be justified, but they should be more interesting than &quot;powerful crazy f*cker who lives in ruins and eats human veal.&quot; There's no person to fight, no flawed thesis to refute, just a rabid animal that walks on two legs and can channel essence. Compelling ideological motivations and formative tragic backstories can still be insufficient justification for monstrous actions and no defense against retribution, but <i>that</i> should be the conclusion we get from Raksi, not &quot;the wyld fucks people up, better put them down quick before they start doing what Raksi does.&quot; A simple human sociopath villain isn't going to have the level of raw power and experience that Raksi has because they've been concerned with small minded immediate self-gratification since the day were born.<br /> <br /> Now, if Raksi in 2e was an active villain, maybe they could have had a message about needing to be vigilant against people like her, but for all her power, she wasn't anything more than a very localized &quot;Conan The Barbarian&quot; villain who spent all of her time bullying local tribes and engaging in navel gazing depravity. She didn't <i>do</i> anything, even cringe inducing 2e Ma-Ha-Suchi led regular raids as far from his lair as Greyfalls. There was no pressing need to fight her unless you wanted the Book of Three Circles. If you didn't need it, you could build up your strength at a leisurely pace and eventually send a magic WMD her way if you wanted her gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T11:08:39-08:00","id":1291885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291870#post1291870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple human sociopath villain isn't going to have the level of raw power and experience that Raksi has because they've been concerned with small minded immediate self-gratification since the day were born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes they're born with a silver spoon in their mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T11:31:30-08:00","id":1291889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291885#post1291885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes they're born with a silver spoon in their mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that's what Dynasts like Tepet Lisara are for. But Raksi clawed her way out of the ruins of the First Age, after the society that worshiped Celestial Exalts as infallible god-monarchs collapsed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:35:36-08:00","id":1291924,"title":"","content":"I was not making a point about Raksi specifically.<br /> <br /> But also, Lunar Exaltation is said to be less concerned with a moral foundation; it might be more accommodating for a person that was already predatory and entitled, and rode the wave of that power into cultivating scenarios to feed their vices.<br /> <br /> Not necessarily Raksi, but still something where I would find a dismissal of &quot;for the evulz&quot; as being too simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:59:20-08:00","id":1291934,"title":"","content":"The Sun may be more impressed with mortals who are passionate in doing what they think is &quot;right&quot;.<br /> <br /> While the Moon may be more impressed with mortals who are most concerned with who will be &quot;left&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:19:40-08:00","id":1291946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291858#post1291858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Restoring Lilith to her First Edition coolness was an important personal goal. You'll see her in Chapter Nine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa, went to bed and got a reply from an actual dev. Can't argue with that! On a happier note regarding Dreams: I understand such an esoteric effect probably a long way off from being designed and won't show up in the book, but as a design concept-going forward are there any plans to implement something like Moon and Earth Song? Always loved the idea of Lunars being able to turn into geographical features.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:02:17-08:00","id":1291975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291946#post1291946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoa, went to bed and got a reply from an actual dev.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go to the thread, there are millions of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T16:31:25-08:00","id":1292006,"title":"","content":"As I've said previously, my problem with Raksi currently is that while you can interact with her (which is a step up from 2e) you realistically would only do it if you had no other option. Putting on a facade of monstrosity only works if it's actually a facade and not who you really are, and in her case she's really just a monster. I think this is <i>why</i> her behavior comes off as 'for the evulz' to me - because the book attempts to convince you that she's just putting on an act and that's not her true personality when it couldn't be further from the truth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T16:48:05-08:00","id":1292011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292006#post1292006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've said previously, my problem with Raksi currently is that while you can interact with her (which is a step up from 2e) you realistically would only do it if you had no other option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could come up with characters that would enthusiastically seek out Raksi's mentorship, and circuitously rationalize anything that she does for the sake of other Lunars that is morally reprehensible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T17:43:26-08:00","id":1292028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1291809#post1291809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're gonna need the Mask of Winters to be a viable mentor for abyssals. So no, they're probably about the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there's a lot of that too. Raksi, Mask, Berit, Chejop. They've all done pretty abominable things in their various long lives, although some worse than others depending on opinions. As PCs you have to deal with them one way or another. You can either be realistic and swallow your concerns for the greater good, for now anyway, or be a hero and punch them in the face. Or something in between.<br /> <br /> I think any splat that realistically has dedicated mentors has that problem. It's fun to deal with though. Luckily they also have the potential for wonderful and wise Shahan-ya, peaceful and learned monks, and enlightened ancient spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T17:52:36-08:00","id":1292030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292011#post1292011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could come up with characters that would enthusiastically seek out Raksi's mentorship, and circuitously rationalize anything that she does for the sake of other Lunars that is morally reprehensible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do that in 2e too. The difference in this edition being you're arguably more of a victim of her sociopathy (or is it psychopathy?) than just being equally as crazy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T17:54:13-08:00","id":1292031,"title":"","content":"One thing I'll say is that the question of how Raksi acts in public (ranging from the general revelry over a debauched court over to occasionally hosting atrocities when holding audience for personal enemies) against her character in private when amongst trusted and valuable company is that it matters less as a subject of assessing moral quality and culpability and more about how people relate to one another. That can make for compelling narratives in a lot of cases, and especially if one is playing the game in a somewhat more melodramatic tone, where the private lives and intimate relationships of the demigod characters can be things of great significance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T18:01:17-08:00","id":1292033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292030#post1292030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could do that in 2e too. The difference in this edition being you're arguably more of a victim of her sociopathy (or is it psychopathy?) than just being equally as crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that in Second Edition, such rationalization was on shakier ground when it was every day with her, rather than when somebody from a contrary faction was around to pay homage.<br /> <br /> I'd certainly say we get a picture of a teacher-student relationship that is generally dysfunctional, but I wouldn't universally characterize that as victimising. Even there, I would regard &quot;rationalizing the worst behaviour of somebody that you're close to or admire makes you another victim&quot; to not only be simplistic, but kind of lets some people off the hook.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm interested in morally judging the fictional characters.<br /> <br /> (Sociopathy and psychopathy are basically equivalent terms, neither is really employed medically or scientifically anymore, and they wouldn't necessarily be well-fitting for Raksi here anyway)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T18:40:53-08:00","id":1292045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292033#post1292033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd certainly say we get a picture of a teacher-student relationship that is generally dysfunctional, but I wouldn't universally characterize that as victimising. Even there, I would regard &quot;rationalizing the worst behaviour of somebody that you're close to or admire makes you another victim&quot; to not only be simplistic, but kind of lets some people off the hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly - hence &quot;arguably&quot; a victim, depending on what level of denial you're going through about who she is and what she's doing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T09:45:07-08:00","id":1292197,"title":"","content":"What Raski's portrayal in 3e says to me is that she is a terrifyingly brilliant person who never does anything for one reason if she can do it for five. One of her major goals, at least as her students are concerned, is very rational. &quot;If you are to join our crusade against the Realm, you are going to need to do terrible things to people, with simple murder being the low end. Better that you get over your squeamishness now than to hesitate later and die to a Wyld Hunt.&quot; Or, to misquote 70 Maxims, &quot;Two Wrongs is <i>Definitely</i> not going to be Enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> The fact that it unsettles her political opponents, makes people worry about what she might do if they oppose her, and allows her to easily take the measure of visitors are also huge benefits. I'm pretty sure she also just straight up enjoys the looks on people's faces.<br /> <br /> And.... Well, my understanding, which may be wrong, is that preindustrial societies tend to have very high infant mortality rates and that some babies might be considered unwanted for various reasons and so might just be left out in the woods. It would feel appropriate to me for Raksi to adopt a &quot;waste not, want not&quot; approach to said unwanted children and, if it makes people think twice about exposing their children, hey that works too.<br /> <br /> As for the seeming contradiction in letting her student have her own way ...well, that's a teachable moment too. First, she was brave enough to stand up to Raksi, which was impressive, so she has some bravery. And second, she also gets to learn that crossing Raksi has consequences, many of which are not immediately obvious.<br /> <br /> And so, after Wenya has spent 12 hours trying to get a crying baby to go to sleep, hasn't slept in days, and hasn't been able to study any occult secrets in weeks, Raksi might come to her and say &quot;Is the life of one mortal worth all this pain? Are you willing to give up on your studies? Or are you going to eat the baby?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or something. Maybe she won't, because she's perfectly fine with just seeing how things turn out (and maybe ending up with a decent Moon Touched lieutenant in a couple of decades).<br /> <br /> Raksi is used to playing the long view and she can probably find a way to turn anything to her advantage eventually.<br /> <br /> Granted, she's not omniscient, and there are significant downsides to having such a fearsome reputation. The situation with her other student might blow up in her face entirely because he's way too scared to actually talk to her, so it's reasonable to wonder just how many &quot;yes men&quot; she has surrounding her and just how much this affects her perception of reality. And ...well, it wouldn't surprise me if she's created some monsters who are even worse than her, people driven to destroy the world. And even if that can be turned to her benefit (pointing them at a target, letting them go, and seeing how many Wyld Hunts they can chew through before they die), I hope she feels some degree of remorse when it happens.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, none of the above makes her any less of a monster. One could argue that it makes her significantly more monstrous that she's rationally planning and carrying out terrible things than if she were a simple beast, lashing out at all who oppose her. But, like people have been saying, having her be a cross between Hermione Granger, Vito Corleone, David Xanatos, and a mythological Rakshasa is much more interesting than having her simply be the Thugee leader from the second Indiana Jones movie or the monster from a slasher film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 02-26-2019, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:40:12-08:00","id":1292214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292197#post1292197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Raski's portrayal in 3e says to me is that she is a terrifyingly brilliant person who never does anything for one reason if she can do it for five. One of her major goals, at least as her students are concerned, is very rational. &quot;If you are to join our crusade against the Realm, you are going to need to do terrible things to people, with simple murder being the low end. Better that you get over your squeamishness now than to hesitate later and die to a Wyld Hunt.&quot; Or, to misquote 70 Maxims, &quot;Two Wrongs is <i>Definitely</i> not going to be Enough.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Probably takes it a bit too far. But I feel as though, out of all the things presented, the one with vivisecting Dynasts might be primarily viewed by other old Lunars as in poor taste more than anything; not a one of them has never vivisected a Dynast themselves, but you don't do that shit in public.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And.... Well, my understanding, which may be wrong, is that preindustrial societies tend to have very high infant mortality rates and that some babies might be considered unwanted for various reasons and so might just be left out in the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the view of babies as adorable is a bit of a historical aberration. For most of history, they've generally been boring, a drain on time and resources, and far too likely to die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, none of the above makes her any less of a monster. One could argue that it makes her significantly more monstrous that she's rationally planning and carrying out terrible things than if she were a simple beast, lashing out at all who oppose her. But, like people have been saying, having her be a cross between Hermione Granger, Vito Corleone, David Xanatos, and a mythological Rakshasa is much more interesting than having her simply be the Thugee leader from the second Indiana Jones movie or the monster from a slasher film.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it helps that she's presented as employing her power to improve the lives of those living under her authority.<br /> <br /> Really, if you're a villain because you do horrible things to your enemies, then something like 80% of everybody ever is a villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T14:27:14-08:00","id":1292266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292214#post1292214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the view of babies as adorable is a bit of a historical aberration. For most of history, they've generally been boring</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T14:42:10-08:00","id":1292267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292266#post1292266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Citation needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how, when you're a subsistence farmer, and the only thing that you can really do with your baby is keep it in a bundle on your back?<br /> <br /> Can't keep them in cribs, because you don't have any. Can't leave work to spend time with them, because nobody really will or can subsidize that. And getting too attached before they display much personality simply isn't practical, because there's something like a forty percent chance that they'll die of disease, exposure (even in your house, it can be cold) or malnutrition before they're two years old.<br /> <br /> Or just being born weak and sickly for reasons including that the parent's diet wasn't exactly rich in vitamins.<br /> <br /> And that's not even considering the documentation of fairly high historical incidences in which babies who were unwanted or inconvenient would just be left out in the wilderness to die. Birth control wasn't very reliable, abortion was likely a disaster and if you weren't really in proximity to a place that took unwanted children in... awful lot of situations in which children come along when they can't be cared for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T17:03:01-08:00","id":1292297,"title":"","content":"I think I see the disconnect here. To me, Raksi's actions do not come off as the actions of someone who sees the bigger picture. They come off as actions of someone who enjoys making others suffer if given the opportunity. Cruelty for cruelty's sake. She vivisects the DB during dinner not as part of some scheme to ferret out his hearth who have infiltrated her domain, but because it hurts both the DB and the people who have to watch. She serves the live baby to the delegate not as a plot to get her new protege to assert herself as well as offer a teachable moment about the consequences of actions, but because she doesn't like the guy.<br /> <br /> The book says she doesn't do any of these things out of sadism (or, more accurately, out of <i>mere</i> sadism), but it does little to convince me that these acts are done out of anything <i>but</i> sadism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T18:26:35-08:00","id":1292317,"title":"","content":"I'm watching a video right now of Elisa Hansen talking about the film Bram Stoker's Dracula. It's starting off with her deconstructing the misconception that Dracula was modelled directly off of Vlad III.<br /> <br /> It puts me in mind of some interesting parallels; a person who, even going past all of the propaganda, probably did some really grotesque things, which has not detracted from an enduring image of being a national hero.<br /> <br /> It raises the question of whether a person who impales several thousand individuals (enemy soldiers, that) to deter possible invaders is doing it because they're cruel, or because it's seen as an effective deterrent under circumstances of limited resources.<br /> <br /> (I observe that subject differently than I would something that happened within the last 150 years)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292297#post1292297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They come off as actions of someone who enjoys making others suffer if given the opportunity. Cruelty for cruelty's sake. She vivisects the DB during dinner not as part of some scheme to ferret out his hearth who have infiltrated her domain, but because it hurts both the DB</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of common throughout the history or warfare; hatred of the enemy, desire to mutilate and humiliate them.<br /> <br /> Franklin Roosevelt was once sent a gift from troops in the Pacific theatre of a letter opened made from the bone of a Japanese soldier.<br /> <br /> Is it cruelty for cruelty's sake, or cruelty for the sake of really hating those people.<br /> <br /> Hell, I wonder if Raksi has an idea of what the Scarlet Empress does with Lunars brought alive into the Imperial Manse. Of all the Silver Pact, she seems like the one best positioned to make a guess. Might not make her very well-disposed towards Dynasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the people who have to watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now I'm thinking of the backstory in which Raksi fought a war against the people who have to watch. In that case, I'm not saying that her attitude towards them is equivalent to the Dynasts with whom she remains at war, but what it says about her views of their philosophies and aspirations. One way to approach it is a view where those things aren't merely different, they're downright dangerous, something that may alternately compromise the Silver Pact or actually make their potential victory pyrrhic. Her actions are still cruel, but could be construed as a motivated cruelty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says she doesn't do any of these things out of sadism (or, more accurately, out of <i>mere</i> sadism), but it does little to convince me that these acts are done out of anything <i>but</i> sadism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on how one defines sadism; it can be a bit of a loaded term, leading to some broader applications than its strict meaning.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T19:57:48-08:00","id":1292344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mmooney</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece#post1291808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...This was a time when Lunars were closer to their cousins in the Old World of Darkness. They could be any sort of animal, sure, but territory was of unparalleled importance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, they were closer to generic pulp barbarian monsters with KotE material hiding under a superficial W:tA gloss. Actually being similar to Garou and Fera is a tall order in Exalted, possibly even untenable, because spirits don't work anywhere remotely in one game as they do in the other; in Werewolf, if the spirit of a river dies, it's goodbye river. Importance of territory was highly tied into this for W:tA, because territory was generally centered around caerns, sacred places where spirit and matter touched, there were generally more spirits hanging out, and hence more important than any one changer's life, or even the life of the entire sept, court, what have you. This isn't really an attitude that's ever cropped up in Exalted, a game where you'll likely often be a ninja interior decorator and a Manse that blows up from Essence buildup or a Demesne that withers until it can't be of use to the Dragon-Blooded anymore is a job well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T09:10:01-08:00","id":1292506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292267#post1292267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know how, when you're a subsistence farmer, and the only thing that you can really do with your baby is keep it in a bundle on your back?<br /> <br /> Can't keep them in cribs, because you don't have any. Can't leave work to spend time with them, because nobody really will or can subsidize that. And getting too attached before they display much personality simply isn't practical, because there's something like a forty percent chance that they'll die of disease, exposure (even in your house, it can be cold) or malnutrition before they're two years old.<br /> <br /> Or just being born weak and sickly for reasons including that the parent's diet wasn't exactly rich in vitamins.<br /> <br /> And that's not even considering the documentation of fairly high historical incidences in which babies who were unwanted or inconvenient would just be left out in the wilderness to die. Birth control wasn't very reliable, abortion was likely a disaster and if you weren't really in proximity to a place that took unwanted children in... awful lot of situations in which children come along when they can't be cared for.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a lot of this is technically true, but it's also part of a once-popular historical theory that's been challenged and largely overturned. I looked at it a bit during my MA. I'm no expert, but I can find some sources. (I remember this because I had an argument with the other students about it!)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yes, some people dumped their children because they couldn't care for them, and society often told parents that, for example, bastards should be handed to monasteries, the disabled should be abandoned, and if your baby died as a child suck it up, because children die all the time.<br /> <br /> Historians Philippe Aries (Centuries of Childhood) and Lawrence Stone (Family, Sex and Marriage in England, 1500-1800) argued that essentially, the Medieval period had no real conception of childhood, and this developed with the creation of the nuclear family in the 18th century, which also encouraged parents to love and care for their babies and children rather than consider them in terms of help for work.<br /> But these were both largely Early Modern historians, and a number of other Early Modernists and medievalists pushed back on this.<br /> <br /> You can read one historians's review of Stone's work for free. Pages 5, 6 and 7 discuss parents not caring that much about their children. Besides history, he argues that sociological studies of families in societies with high infant mortality today show that, in fact, it's really upsetting to lose an infant.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.alanmacfarlane.com/TEXTS/stonesex.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.alanmacfarlane.com/TEXTS/stonesex.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.alanmacfarlane.com/TEXTS/stonesex.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.alanmacfarlane.com/TEXTS/stonesex.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Shulamith Shahar (Childhood in the Middle Ages), Barbara Hanawult (The Ties that Bound: Peasant Families in Medieval England) argue that most of the historical evidence actually shows that individuals, by and large, actually did really care about their babies, and were often devastated by their deaths*.<br /> <br /> A more recent book I've heard good things about is Elisheva Baumgarten, Mothers and Children: Jewish Family Life in Medieval Europe, which also argues the same thing. One thing she found is that Jewish authories often complained of how many men were depressed and crying about their dead babies, and how they needed to get over it.<br /> So there's a disconnect between the unemotional views of society (babies die all the time, it's not a big deal) and the individual experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Though I suppose society had means of helping them cope that are not so available to families today; firstly, that most people had relatives who'd been through the same thing (I remember my mum found it really difficult losing two babies and then her mum partly because none of her friends had the same experience), and second, a strong belief in the afterlife.<br /> Hildegard of Bremen, the famous medieval prophetess, received many letters from mothers asking if she had seen their dead babies in Heaven (and she often wrote back saying that, yes, don't worry, your baby is in Heaven). There's also the phenomon where midwives often told the parents of stillbirths that their child had been alive for 20 seconds... just long enough for an emergency baptism before dying, so again, at least they're in Heaven. (see Ronald Finucane &quot;The Rescue of Innocents&quot;)<br /> <br /> For the end, here's the epigraph of a five-year old Roman slave child. Older than a baby, admittedly, but still young enough to be a burden and have a high chance of death. Apparently the Latin really conveys the owner's (not even her real father!) sadness.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Here I commend to you, Fronto and Flaccilla,<br /> your daughter, my joy and my delight,<br /> Let young Erotion not be terrified by the black shades<br /> and the gaping mouth of the Tartarian dog.<br /> She would have completed six cold winters,<br /> had she only lived but six more days.<br /> Let her play happily between her aged parents,<br /> and chatter my name with her lisping voice.<br /> Let the turf covering her bones be soft and not hard,<br /> and do not weigh heavily on that girl, Mother Earth,<br /> For she was not heavy on you.</div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Tldr; people knew to expect high infant mortality, and authorities often told people to just buck up, but individuals were often greatly saddened by the early deaths of their children. Sure, some dumped them, but that doesn't mean most people weren't upset by it (and of course, people who dumped them were still often upset, even if they felt it was necessary; how many women today who give up babies for adoption feel entirely happy about it?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-27-2019, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T09:57:07-08:00","id":1292523,"title":"","content":"I'm picturing all of those Mafia shows/movies, where the Don does despicable things to (in their mind) keep the organization running, but then is the loving grandpa at home, just with a slathering of millennia old magic demi-monster-demi-god jadedness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T10:56:56-08:00","id":1292533,"title":"","content":"I'll try tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:25:32-08:00","id":1292546,"title":"","content":"So, anyhow.<br /> <br /> What is Raksi's purpose in the setting?<br /> <br /> In one sense, she's the stereotype that the Realm points to; Anathema are bloodthirsty monsters, who literally <i>eat babies</i>.<br /> <br /> So she's important in allowing the Realm's system of oppression a bit more complex; when they say the Anathema are evil, it's not total rubbish.<br /> <br /> But villains are boring when they're utterly one-dimensional (and &quot;she's evil because she's crazy!&quot; is pretty one-dimensional); and they're also unbelievable. Most tyrants have support from at least some of the populace. I remember talking to a Syrian refugee (a guy who wouldn't go back to Syria because he'd be press-ganged into the army) who felt that Western media is very biased against Assad. Of course, Assad does bad things... but he protects people from ISIS, Al-Nusra, etc.<br /> <br /> Raksi controls a large territory, with many loyal tribes, human and beastmen. If they obeyed her purely out of fear, it might come off as a bit unrealistic, and of course it would be far too easy for DB PCs to foment an uprising.<br /> Even villains need true believers.<br /> <br /> So Raksi needs to be not 100% evil. So why do people support her?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It puts me in mind of some interesting parallels; a person who, even going past all of the propaganda, probably did some really grotesque things, which has not detracted from an enduring image of being a national hero.<br /> <br /> It raises the question of whether a person who impales several thousand individuals (enemy soldiers, that) to deter possible invaders is doing it because they're cruel, or because it's seen as an effective deterrent under circumstances of limited resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the most likely. Raksi makes her tribes strong, she defends them against their enemies, including the Realm (operating, I guess, from Greyfalls), which considers them heathens deserving of nothing but slavery, or Lookshy who considers them dangerous barbarians who threaten the Confederation of Rivers.<br /> <br /> Yes, they have to sacrifice a few babies to their terrifying goddess (though I wonder if many of the babies are stolen from other tribes), and that's painful, but it has to be done for the greater good. And no doubt their society has been influenced and structured over generations to reinforce this &quot;honour&quot; and &quot;harsh necessity&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mentioned that's one place for her...<br /> Her other place in the setting is as a mentor for Lunar sorcerers. There's even an initiation for it.<br /> And her being so monstrous (and she is; yes the baby-eating may be calculated, but it's still clearly wrong, as the story of her adherant who complained shows other Lunars are aware) may seem problematic...<br /> <br /> But then, the Core book has an initiation for Solars where they learn dark magicks from a demon (and not even a simply alien demon, but a soul-sucking, doom-loving demon), and this is basically the Lunar equivalent. If you don't want to play a sorcerer who made dark pacts for their powers, talk to a nice ghost at sunset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-27-2019, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:28:46-08:00","id":1292547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292546#post1292546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even villains need true believers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counselor Palpatine (later Emperor Palpatine) sure did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:35:29-08:00","id":1292551,"title":"","content":"Indeed. His lieutenant, the scared politicians who voted him in, the soldiers who fought his wars, the citizens who paid taxes without rioting.<br /> <br /> There's a very good bit at the beginning of one of the Star Wars rpg books (Dawn of Rebellion, I think) about how the citizens of the Inner Core mostly believe the Empire is a great and good force, even if they grumble at high taxes.<br /> <br /> Hey, I lived in a dictatorship that oppresses minorities and cracks down on dissent for four years (they have literal concentration camps where they're attempting to destroy an entire culture); most people shrug and get on with it. And there's plenty who genuinely believe that Xi JinPing is a strong leader who's cracking down on corruption and standing up for China. Sure, they admit there's issues, it's not perfect... but what government is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T12:27:49-08:00","id":1292569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292546#post1292546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, anyhow.<br /> <br /> What is Raksi's purpose in the setting?<br /> <br /> In one sense, she's the stereotype that the Realm points to; Anathema are bloodthirsty monsters, who literally <i>eat babies</i>.<br /> <br /> So she's important in allowing the Realm's system of oppression a bit more complex; when they say the Anathema are evil, it's not total rubbish.<br /> <br /> But villains are boring when they're utterly one-dimensional (and &quot;she's evil because she's crazy!&quot; is pretty one-dimensional); and they're also unbelievable. Most tyrants have support from at least some of the populace. I remember talking to a Syrian refugee (a guy who wouldn't go back to Syria because he'd be press-ganged into the army) who felt that Western media is very biased against Assad. Of course, Assad does bad things... but he protects people from ISIS, Al-Nusra, etc.<br /> <br /> Raksi controls a large territory, with many loyal tribes, human and beastmen. If they obeyed her purely out of fear, it might come off as a bit unrealistic, and of course it would be far too easy for DB PCs to foment an uprising.<br /> Even villains need true believers.<br /> <br /> So Raksi needs to be not 100% evil. So why do people support her?<br /> <br /> <br /> I think this is the most likely. Raksi makes her tribes strong, she defends them against their enemies, including the Realm (operating, I guess, from Greyfalls), which considers them heathens deserving of nothing but slavery, or Lookshy who considers them dangerous barbarians who threaten the Confederation of Rivers.<br /> <br /> Yes, they have to sacrifice a few babies to their terrifying goddess (though I wonder if many of the babies are stolen from other tribes), and that's painful, but it has to be done for the greater good. And no doubt their society has been influenced and structured over generations to reinforce this &quot;honour&quot; and &quot;harsh necessity&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mentioned that's one place for her...<br /> Her other place in the setting is as a mentor for Lunar sorcerers. There's even an initiation for it.<br /> And her being so monstrous (and she is; yes the baby-eating may be calculated, but it's still clearly wrong, as the story of her adherant who complained shows other Lunars are aware) may seem problematic...<br /> <br /> But then, the Core book has an initiation for Solars where they learn dark magicks from a demon (and not even a simply alien demon, but a soul-sucking, doom-loving demon), and this is basically the Lunar equivalent. If you don't want to play a sorcerer who made dark pacts for their powers, talk to a nice ghost at sunset.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She's also sincerely supports Lunar autonomy. She honestly respects the idea that every Lunar has the right to run things how they want; she hates Ma-Ha-Suchi because he disagrees politically with her on that. So she's a person who honestly isn't out to be domineering towards people who don't mess with her first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T13:24:00-08:00","id":1292587,"title":"","content":"That's quite true. As a Lunar, unless you want to study under her, she's easy to avoid.<br /> <br /> One of my players was a Lunar who trained under her, left, and... never came back. That wasn't a big deal. She was pissed at him about something else (he lost her peach of immortality, so later she made him steal another one for her), but not about leaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T15:47:00-08:00","id":1292631,"title":"","content":"I personally read Raksi's ideology as being less focused on self-determination and more on a sense that holding all of Creation under a large, interconnected system makes it too vulnerable to large-scale collapse from something going wrong in a given sector, and she argues that greater provincial independence allows the system as a whole to be more robust against breakdowns or invasions of any given sector.<br /> <br /> Mostly because I want there to be <i>somebody</i> in the setting who believes that. I'm not sure if there are any stray details in her associated write-ups that might contradict that.<br /> <br /> One implication I think it would have would be Raksi being somewhat less concerned with their freedom than their responsibilities as she judges them; she wants them to govern independently from one another, but she also wants them to govern. Not necessarily confined indefinitely to their own principalities, but still reprimanded if they skip out on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T20:37:26-08:00","id":1292690,"title":"","content":"I have some thoughts about how to assess Raksi and tie a lot of it together, but before getting into that (which should wait until the morning), I want to nip something in the bed.<br /> <br /> Yes, Wizard effectively counterargued a point that I swung about a bit, and it would be immature and cowardly of me to not acknowledge that and take it into proper future considerations. It was a perspective held partially based on some research from a couple of years back, but I would be remiss in not admitting that it was one I was really kind of attached to from a desire for some intellectual superiority and a bit of shock value. That's a lingering flaw in me, and effective corrections have value in that in addition to generally expanding my perspective, which is a thing I try to appreciate in its own right.<br /> <br /> So... thanks. Sincerely. And good on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T22:59:48-08:00","id":1292705,"title":"","content":"Ohoho Lord. I still have a wider thing to say about Raksi, but I just had a notion that is just too delicious.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't characterise Raksi as cruel in the sense that she gets gratification from the suffering of others... but I'd just bet that she really likes feeling as though she's the smartest one in the room, and that she's got everybody else figured out.<br /> <br /> If I was behind her words, I would have it be that the ultimate reason that she made the student who spoke out against her the caregiver of the saved baby was because she thought that shit was really clever.<br /> <br /> And her putting on appalling shows... might be the Exalted exaggeration of somebody who would be partially motivated to say &quot;people before the 19th century didn't value children until they could walk and talk&quot; out of a desire for some smug cleverness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T23:33:18-08:00","id":1292710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292631#post1292631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally read Raksi's ideology as being less focused on self-determination and more on a sense that holding all of Creation under a large, interconnected system makes it too vulnerable to large-scale collapse from something going wrong in a given sector, and she argues that greater provincial independence allows the system as a whole to be more robust against breakdowns or invasions of any given sector.<br /> <br /> Mostly because I want there to be <i>somebody</i> in the setting who believes that. I'm not sure if there are any stray details in her associated write-ups that might contradict that.<br /> <br /> One implication I think it would have would be Raksi being somewhat less concerned with their freedom than their responsibilities as she judges them; she wants them to govern independently from one another, but she also wants them to govern. Not necessarily confined indefinitely to their own principalities, but still reprimanded if they skip out on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point. One world government isn't practical in the age of the internet, let alone the age of sorrows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T03:43:00-08:00","id":1292723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292710#post1292710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One world government isn't practical in the age of the internet</div> </div> </div> </div>The age of the Internet is one in which we're more interconnected and interdependent than ever, there are so many social and economic systems that could experience complete disaster if the wrong server farm goes up in smoke.<br /> <br /> Look at some of the fears around Brexit; one country pulls off a poorly considered and short-sighted referendum, three years later it's facing a major severance from an important common market which could have ruinous consequences for its own economy, and being one of the largest and most important ones in the world, that would have major knock on effects to drag several others down with it.<br /> <br /> I've not yet seen The Big Short, but I know that it goes into the details of how an American housing crisis turned into a worldwide economic disaster.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T09:03:09-08:00","id":1292781,"title":"","content":"Okay, so my overall assessment of Raksi with the available details before she gets a write-up in the later chapter.<br /> <br /> First off, the line about her revelling in being herself. That's capping off a description of how she's had to change in the Second Age, specifically the activities in opposition to the Realm. That reads to me as heavily focused on the matter that the terrible things that she's had to (or opted to) do in the course of battling the enemies of the Silver Pact, in contrast to her more scholastic and contemplative nature in the comfort of the latter First Age, is not something for which she feels any kind of conflict. She'd wake a sleeping behemoth and direct it at coastal towns of the Blessed Isle, and not lament what cruel fate has forced her to sully herself with; she'd think that she's pretty awesome. In that, she's probably not very different from a lot of Lunars, just standing out heavily from the fact that she's experienced a transition from the time when the Lunars were more persecuted. I don't even think she's particularly vengeful towards the Usurpation; I'd say that, at best, she views her activities against the Realm as pragmatic necessities to preserve her own sovereignty and fight for the future she wishes to build, at less than best she thinks that being thrust into this conflict has allowed her to find her best self.<br /> <br /> Okay, the general situation of what is and is not an act; put a pin on what she exposes her opposition to for the moment. The overall characterisation of Raksi's court is presented as one of hedonism and decadence, unrestrained extravagance. That's the public face, that's what a majority of fellow Lunars see. The general assessment of Raksi's character is probably that she views her domain as a source of pleasures to indulge herself in, and even when there might be some discerning enough to assess that it's so showy that it comes off as trying too hard, they're uncertain about where such artifice ends and where Raksi's true pleasures begin.<br /> <br /> Even the displays she puts on for the benefit of opponents are probably generally framed and received as that pursuit of hedonism extended beyond the limits of reason and decency, as well as with the actual intention to shock and outrage. I would even imagine that a lot of people who experience that know that the intent is to get a rise out of them, and figure the best way to get a reprieve for themselves and any unfortunate victims is to put up a front of being unmoved, or even finding it predictable and pass\u00e9. I still imagine that in a lot of cases, such a thing won't work, because I'm guessing Raksi has good Perception and is good at figuring out the true feelings of people before her; whether a visitor takes her more extreme displays at face value or recognises it as something intended to provoke, if they try to affect disinterest and Raksi sees through that, the game probably shifts to trying to break down their fa\u00e7ade for all to see.<br /> <br /> So that's the face. What about the Raksi beneath?<br /> <br /> Per the information conveyed, the hedonism itself isn't the point for her, and she could probably internally manage without it. It itself is not actually gratifying for her, and she wouldn't be moved by its absence. Likewise, the displays of cruelty aren't about sadism in the sense of her experiencing an emotional gratification directly in the pain or disgust of others.<br /> <br /> Rather, I would view Raksi's gratifications in activities of dominance, and in displays of her intellect and prowess. In constructing her court, the gratification isn't in the revelries it entails, but having put together and managed such a fa\u00e7ade that people who want to truly engage her are forced to navigate through (and probably a bit of gratification for experiencing peerage when somebody actually does have the wit to see through it all, or impresses her enough to bring the walls down). In other cases, her exertions of dominance are amoral; she's extravagantly generous to friends, adherents, worshippers, and utterly merciless in the face of enemies and ideological rivals. Part of the significance of a difference between act and truth is that it can cause even adherents to misjudge her; the likes of Dark Eyes think she's as temperamental as the persona she puts on in public, and so try to act in her blind spots, unaware that her genuine priorities would actually enjoy some of their achievements.<br /> <br /> Probably not in an empathetic sense, but rather an aesthetic admiration. In cases where she acts in accordance with her true priorities rather than what would be consistent with the persona, people not in the know probably judge her as mercurial and move on.<br /> <br /> In a lot of this, Raksi would not be very different from many other fictional depictions, or some real life speculations, on autocrats, where the pageantry of their officer and cruelty of their &quot;justice&quot; doesn't really reflect their real inner life or private moments, and in cases where they don't find it soul-draining, they at least find it exhausting to maintain the fa\u00e7ade. I once read a semi-fictional account of an Ottoman sultan, in which he felt a wearisome obligation to have sex with a newly provided member of the harem when all he really wanted to do was read his books, because to not do so could generate rumours of impotence that would weaken his standing in court.<br /> <br /> What I find interesting with Raksi is the idea that she is not exhausted or conflicted in the falsehoods she spins about herself, because for her the energy expended is the point, is its own reward. I don't think you get many depictions of a character like that.<br /> <br /> As for whether or not she's a villain, I think one thing that complicates that if one is playing a member of the Silver Pact is that Raksi is truly on your side. Not like some villains where their assistance is a side effect of something that fulfils their own agenda, and the seemingly mutual relationship is ultimately exploitative of the less evil person, I'm reading Raksi as sincerely believing in her vision for the future of Creation. Not necessarily driven by a moral imperative, or even the needs for her own personal security (which she seems to have covered already), she just finds it a worthwhile and beneficial endeavour.<br /> <br /> So one thing that any Lunars who find her truly repellent would need to process is the matter of how she's still a really useful person to have in their cause, and that the benefits she's brought are actually something that fourth generation Lunars on the whole have been privileged by. Even leaving aside babies, there's no ethical consumption under Raksi. I actually think that can be a more compelling moral subject to grapple with than pursuing the conclusion that Raksi is evil to the point of casting her down in some fashion.<br /> <br /> What I think might really bake the noodle of some Lunars is the possibility that Raksi could genuinely sacrifice her own life in the service or safeguarding of other Lunars. Probably not go out of her way for it, but there may be circumstances in which, faced with a trolley problem in which the trolley is a really powerful Sidereal-backed Wyld Hunt, she'd turn that trolley on herself with the same gusto with which she seems to pursue everything. If she thought that doing so could better safeguard a world in which her vision for Lunar supremacy could come to pass, and where she gets to go out on her own terms and with one last grand feat to her name... she might just do it.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps if she got a good shot at Chejop Kejak, and has judged that the chance that she'd die was not massively weighted against the chance that she'd kill him, I think it's conceivable that she could go for that from desire to remove a major opponent of the Pact.<br /> <br /> A lot of this is still provisional. What I'm really excited to see are her Intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T10:52:34-08:00","id":1292811,"title":"","content":"So in other words, when Raksi left the screaming match with Ma-Ha-Suchi, as the Silver Pact just looked at her with disgust and horror, she left with an invocation of &quot;Say goodnight to the bad guy!&quot;?<br /> <br /> I don't have any problems with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T11:23:53-08:00","id":1292818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292811#post1292811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in other words, when Raksi left the screaming match with Ma-Ha-Suchi, as the Silver Pact just looked at her with disgust and horror, she left with an invocation of &quot;Say goodnight to the bad guy!&quot;?<br /> <br /> I don't have any problems with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that this is a reference to something, and I can't fully parse it on that.<br /> <br /> I have a notion in which Raksi's domain is one in which, something like once a week, the people within her border get to go before her throne and make direct petitions to her; not everybody gets to go at once, but there's something in place to try and ensure people with pressing needs aren't left for a week.<br /> <br /> A family might come before her, begging for help, as their eldest son, a previously strapping young lad, has developed a big lump in the middle of his back, his legs are no longer working, and his sight seems to be going the same way.<br /> <br /> Raksi immediately descends from her throne, reaches into the boy's back, and bloodlessly rips the tumour right out of him, and already he reports that some of the feeling is starting to come back. Sure, she could have done it in a less dramatic and somewhat extreme way (and a lot of the time probably does), but the mood took her.<br /> <br /> And in that moment, her thoughts won't be with how all of her petitioners and guards and courtiers go to their knees in awe of her. They won't be on how that family will be back in another week to make an offering of some rare game animal, or sweet papayas from their own grove, or some piece of jewellery they lovingly crafted (although she'll graciously accept those things, because waste not, and besides they actually are delicious).<br /> <br /> They'll be on that tumour in her hand, and they'll be something approximately like &quot;yeah, fuck cancer, woo!&quot;<br /> <br /> Later on she'll grow that tumour into a meat dragon, that she'll chase over to perform a raid on Greyfalls, having instilled in it an instinct to attack expensive or irreplaceable infrastructure (although not the war manse, it's too well-protected for what this creature can do and would waste the effort of making it), and ensures that it sees Dragon Blooded with her face in an expression suggesting vulnerability (it probably won't survive against as many as are in Greyfalls, but it will definitely at least maim a few of them enough to be sent home for costly treatments, and might even take a few down with it), and her thoughts won't really be on the terror and disgust and the screams of pain, they'll be on another job well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T12:43:39-08:00","id":1292832,"title":"","content":"It's a reference to Tony Montana, from Scarface (the 80s version). He makes that a centerpiece of a drunken rant aimed at everyone in a resteraunt who just saw his girlfriend break up with him, pointing out he knows he's at fault and owns his darkness, as opposed to everyone else thinking they can blame their problems on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T13:27:36-08:00","id":1292845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292832#post1292832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a reference to Tony Montana, from Scarface (the 80s version). He makes that a centerpiece of a drunken rant aimed at everyone in a resteraunt who just saw his girlfriend break up with him, pointing out he knows he's at fault and owns his darkness, as opposed to everyone else thinking they can blame their problems on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I've only ever seen something like the last third of that movie, and that was <i>ages</i> ago. The start of that scene might have been the point at which I tuned in.<br /> <br /> In any case, I would draw a distinction, because I don't see Raksi having any issue with the circumstances of her life, and she kind of comes across as more stable than Montana does. I would imagine her derision in a similar scenario to be more chipper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T17:07:06-08:00","id":1292884,"title":"","content":"So a Dexter Style Sociopath who depending on your allegiance probably works for everyone\u2019s greater good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T17:32:36-08:00","id":1292887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291808-third-edition-raksi-less-monstrous-but-far-more-villainous-an-opinion-piece?p=1292884#post1292884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Dexter Style Sociopath who depending on your allegiance probably works for everyone\u2019s greater good?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nnnot really.<br /> <br /> For one thing, what is a sociopath?<br /> <br /> For another, Dexter's actions were portrayed as being driven by an indelible impulse to kill, that he was basically taught to mythologize by doing in accordance to standards of permission from his father figure. He's not... in a war. Against, like, the whole United States. He also doesn't really proactively do beneficial things for other people, at least not often.<br /> <br /> I think that Raksi could effectively get through the rest of her life if all of her goals that were opposed by other great powers were accomplished. Spends the remainder of her life asserting her power by manufacturing wonder in her domain, studying her troves of sorcerous lore, and contemplating the deep esoteric mysteries.<br /> <br /> I'm not suggesting that killing, in and of itself, fulfils something for her emotionally, but rather than being in the situation of a war like this means that a core personality trait of revelling in dominating applications of her intellect means that she engages in the violence with gusto.<br /> <br /> If I was going to compare her to any fictional property, I guess... I could kind of see something comparable in her to the Benedict Cumberbatch Sherlock series, in which she's both Sherlock and Moriarty simultaneously, except a Sherlock whose revelry in intellectual exercise includes creative outlets that benefit people, and a Moriarty whose involvement in criminality is owed to an inherent deviance and general bored detachment from life.<br /> <br /> Again, all very provisional. Really want to see her Intimacies.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Alternatively, she's like a differently egotistical, anti-globalist version of Doctor Doom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-28-2019, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T18:25:13-08:00","id":1292900,"title":"","content":"I want to note that since it's very new, I'm still getting all of the details of what we have so far straight in my head.<br /> <br /> To whit, per the description in the book, Raksi's meat dragon days are mostly behind her, with more dedication given to her tumour removal (which she probably had less time for when she was dedicated to making meat dragons), and at least part of the reason for cultivating her current image of hedonistic excess is to keep the memory of her reputation from those days alive, in the hopes that it will inspire the next generation of front line Lunars to make their own meat dragons.<br /> <br /> And to condition them more directly, for any of them who heard stories of that orb thing with the nerves, that electrocuted people and ate their skin, and decide they'd very much like to learn to make or find things like that for themselves; Raksi's going to do her level best to be an object lesson to ensure that they actually have the will to employ such things once they know everything she has to teach about them.<br /> <br /> She could probably do more if she wasn't really embittered about her falling out with Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2026 which is now making me think that part of why she maintains the hedonistic image is that she's just proud enough to want her peers to think that she's withdrawing into her secured domain to just indulge monstrous appetites, rather than because she's nursing hurts from the messy end of a dear friendship.<br /> <br /> Which all rolls back to the point of Raksi still ultimately being a jerk, because of what some of this says about her priorities, but still a jerk motivated by big melodramatic feelings rather than intrinsically anti-social and lacking in empathy or remorse. Other Lunars, possibly playable Lunars, might be varying degrees of jerks themselves in how much latitude they give her should they be allowed in.<br /> <br /> Hmm, some of these considerations might be cause to revise the idea that Raksi's magnanimous rule is driven by gratification from exertions of power and intellect alone. I mean, even within that model, there was still a consideration for the idea that having a category of people to be generous to in the first place implies some sense of investment in either the well-being of certain people, or the value of Lunars as a positive ruling force. It just might be that proactive empathy figures in a bit more than I was initially considering. <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that one could probably make an interesting story out of how either Raksi or Ma-Ha-Suchi responds to the other being killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}